.TH ORO-TEST-DOM-HELPERS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:test/dom\-helpers \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:test/dom\-helpers'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Provides a test runner for Oro Runtime.
.PP
Example usage: import { test } from 'oro:test/dom\-helpers.js'
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBtoElement(selector)\fR
Converts querySelector string to an HTMLElement or validates an existing HTMLElement.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIselector\fR (string \\| Element; required) A CSS selector string, or an instance of HTMLElement, or Element.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIElement\fR The HTMLElement, Element, or Window that corresponds to the selector.
.TP
\fBwaitFor(args, lambda)\fR
Waits for an element to appear in the DOM and resolves the promise when it does.
.br
waitFor({ selector: '#my\-element', visible: true, timeout: 5000 }) .then(el => console.log('Element found:', el)) .catch(err => console.log('Element not found:', err));
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIargs\fR (Object; required) Configuration arguments.
.br
\fIargs.selector\fR (string; optional) The CSS selector to look for.
.br
\fIargs.visible\fR (boolean; optional; default true) Whether the element should be visible.
.br
\fIargs.timeout\fR (number; optional; default defaultTimeout) Time in milliseconds to wait before rejecting the promise.
.br
\fIlambda\fR (() => HTMLElement \\| Element \\| null \\| undefined; optional) An optional function that returns the element. Used if the `selector` is not provided.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Element \\| HTMLElement \\| void>\fR A promise that resolves to the found element.
.TP
\fBwaitForText(args)\fR
Waits for an element's text content to match a given string or regular expression.
.br
waitForText({ element: document.body, text: 'Hello', timeout: 5000 }) .then(el => console.log('Element found:', el)) .catch(err => console.log('Element not found:', err));
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIargs\fR (Object; required) Configuration arguments.
.br
\fIargs.element\fR (Element; required) The root element from which to begin searching.
.br
\fIargs.text\fR (string; optional) The text to search for within elements.
.br
\fIargs.regex\fR (RegExp; optional) A regular expression to match against element text content.
.br
\fIargs.multipleTags\fR (boolean; optional; default false) Whether to look for text across multiple sibling elements.
.br
\fIargs.timeout\fR (number; optional; default defaultTimeout) Time in milliseconds to wait before rejecting the promise.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Element \\| HTMLElement \\| void>\fR A promise that resolves to the found element or null.
.TP
\fBevent(args)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIargs\fR (Object; required) Arguments
.br
\fIargs.event\fR (string \\| Event; required) The event to dispatch.
.br
\fIargs.element\fR (HTMLElement \\| Element \\| window; optional; default window) The element to dispatch the event on.
.TP
\fBisElementVisible(element, previousElement)\fR
Copy pasted from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/testing\-library/jest\-dom/master/src/to\-be\-visible.js
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIelement\fR (Element \\| HTMLElement; required)
.br
\fIpreviousElement\fR (Element \\| HTMLElement; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
